  "findings": "Replaced invalid genus/azalea references with actual ponticum May photographs including known wild-origin RBGE19851065B. Dedicated long evergreen terminal leaves and purple funnel trusses follow branching stems. First pilot too sparse; increased older foliage along shoots and varied leaf droop. Current roughly 1.7-3.6 m family includes dense small and open spreading mature shrubs. Existing lilac palette is less saturated than source magenta; no global palette change made. Petal microdetail omitted at 25 mm. Actually reviewed final seeds 1,4,7 and all 36 variants after refactoring. Accepted stylized spring source; user endorsement remains separate.",
